+5. When asked to open or update a PR, identify the actual upstream repository, source remote and its repository owner, head branch, and explicit base; confirm the base and head exist on their intended remotes. Do not infer the source owner from a branch-name prefix. Run `gh pr list --head <branch> --repo <owner/repo> --state open --json number,url,headRefName,headRepositoryOwner,baseRefName` first. The branch filter cannot distinguish forks: match `headRepositoryOwner.login`, `headRefName` and `baseRefName` against the intended source owner, head branch and explicit base before selecting a PR. Edit the single exact match by explicit number and target repository with `gh pr edit <number> --repo <owner/repo>`. If metadata is missing or several exact matches remain, retain the draft and report the ambiguity instead of guessing. If no exact match exists, create a PR with the explicit target repository, source head/fork and base; do not edit another owner's PR or a PR with a different base. Push only when explicitly requested. If the branch is not available remotely, report that blocker and retain the draft.
